;;; padsynth.xtm -- lush pads, string ensembles and choirs from PADsynth tables

;; Author: Ben Swift
;; Keywords: extempore

;;; Commentary:

;; A pad instrument built on the PADsynth method, which is Paul Nasca's. This
;; is an independent implementation, written from a description of the method
;; and not from any existing program's source.
;;
;; The usual way to make a sustained tone is to add up sine waves, one per
;; harmonic, each at an exact frequency. Real ensembles aren't like that. Ten
;; violinists playing the same A are each a few cents out, and each wavers a
;; little, so what reaches the ear at "the second harmonic" isn't one line in
;; the spectrum but a narrow hump of energy a few hertz wide. PADsynth builds
;; that hump directly. For every harmonic it writes a bell-shaped (Gaussian)
;; band of magnitudes into one very long spectrum, gives every bin of the
;; spectrum its own random phase, and runs a single inverse FFT. Out comes a
;; sample several seconds long which already sounds like many players.
;;
;; Why it works: a band B Hz wide made of many bins with random phases is a
;; sinusoid whose amplitude and phase wander at random, at rates up to about B
;; Hz. That's what the sum of several slightly detuned, slowly drifting copies
;; of a partial sounds like too: it beats, swells and fades, never quite
;; repeating. So a band of a few hertz is an ensemble's "chorus" for that
;; harmonic, without any oscillators or delay lines.
;;
;; Why the band should widen with the harmonic: if each player is out by a
;; few cents, that's the same few cents at every harmonic, and a cent is a
;; fixed fraction of the frequency. So the band's width in hertz grows in
;; proportion to the harmonic's number. Here a band's width is
;;
;;   W = (2^(cents/1200) - 1) * f0 * r^p
;;
;; for a partial at r times the fundamental f0. With p = 1 every partial is
;; equally wide in cents, like a real section. A little above 1 lets the top
;; partials smear further (the shimmer of a big string section); p = 0 makes
;; them all equally wide in hertz, so the upper partials of the organ stay
;; steady and only its lowest pipes move.
;;
;; Every band carries the same power whatever its width: a wide band is
;; lower at its peak than a narrow one. Overlapping bands add in power, which
;; is right for things with independent random phases.
;;
;; The spectrum is also shaped by a fixed curve in absolute hertz, the same
;; for every note, which is how a choir gets its vowel. A voice's vocal tract
;; has resonances (formants) at fixed frequencies --- for "ah" around 700 and
;; 1100 Hz, for "oo" around 320 and 800 Hz --- whatever note is sung. So the
;; tables here are built with the formants applied to each partial at its own
;; frequency in hertz: a low note has many partials under each formant and a
;; high one few, and the vowel stays the same up and down the keyboard. The
;; formants move a little from a low-voice set to a high-voice set between C3
;; and C5, so low notes sound like tenors and basses and high ones like altos
;; and sopranos. The string timbres use the same idea with broad body
;; resonances in place of vowels.
;;
;; How the tables are made and played. An inverse FFT's output is circular:
;; its last sample runs straight on into its first, so a table loops with no
;; seam and needs no crossfade. Each table is 2^17 = 131 072 samples (about
;; three seconds) and stored as 16-bit integers with one gain per table, so
;; the whole bank fits in about 29 MB. There are eight timbres (below), each
;; built at fourteen key zones half an octave apart, from C1 to F#7: 112
;; tables. Each zone's base frequency is moved slightly (by up to 25 cents)
;; so that it falls exactly on a bin of the spectrum which is a multiple of
;; four; then every harmonic, and the sub-octave and fifth used by the organ,
;; land exactly on an even bin, and the tables are perfectly in tune. A zone
;; holds nothing above about 14 kHz, so it can be read up to half an octave
;; sharp without the sound itself folding over. (The cubic read adds faint
;; images of strong high lines; the glass and organ, which are made of lines,
;; stop at 8.8 kHz to keep those quiet.)
;;
;; A note reads the two zones either side of its pitch, at the speed which
;; puts it in tune, and crossfades between them with equal-power weights (the
;; two tables are unrelated noise, so their powers add). It reads the selected
;; timbre and the next one in the bank too, and `morph` crossfades between
;; them. The left and right channels read the same table half a loop apart,
;; which gives two uncorrelated signals for any band wider than about a
;; hertz: a wide stereo image for free. A narrow partial on an even bin is in
;; phase half a loop later, so the narrow low partials (the fundamental of
;; the dark sub, the organ's pipes) stay in the centre and never cancel in
;; mono. Reading starts at a random point for each note, so repeated notes
;; never sound the same.
;;
;; The tables are built when the first padsynth track is made, with an
;; inverse FFT written out below, and are shared by every padsynth track.
;; Building them takes about a third of a second; they live outside the
;; track's memory zone, and stay for the rest of the session.
;;
;; After the tables, each voice has a 12 dB/octave lowpass filter with its
;; own envelope, an amplitude envelope, a delayed vibrato, and two slow random
;; drifts: one in pitch, one in `morph`, so a held chord breathes between
;; neighbouring timbres.
;;
;; The timbres, in the order `morph` moves through them:
;;
;;   0 strings    a focused ensemble core with a wide, shimmering halo
;;   1 ensemble   a brighter string-machine ensemble with a lift at 3 kHz
;;   2 ah         a choir singing "ah"
;;   3 oo         a choir singing "oo"
;;   4 air        a hollow, blurred tone almost dissolved in breath
;;   5 glass      a stretched, nearly sinusoidal tone plus the inharmonic
;;                partials of a vibrating bar: a glass bell
;;   6 organ      drawbar pipes with very narrow bands
;;   7 sub        a soft, triangle-like tone with a sub-octave

;;; Code:

(sys:load-preload-check 'studio-padsynth)
(define *xtmlib-studio-padsynth-loaded* #t)

(sys:load "libs/studio/api.xtm")
(sys:load "libs/studio/dsp.xtm")

(def-instrument padsynth
  "PADsynth pads: string ensembles, choirs, glass and organ from long, looping spectral tables"
  (params
    (timbre 0.0 "which table set, 0 to 7: strings, ensemble, ah, oo, air, glass, organ, sub (taken at note-on)")
    (morph 0.0 "crossfade towards the next timbre, 0.0 to 1.0")
    (level 1.0 "output level, linear (1.0 is the reference level)")
    (attack 0.8 "seconds to swell to full level")
    (decay 2.0 "seconds to fall 60 dB towards the sustain level")
    (sustain 1.0 "level held after the decay, 0.0 to 1.0")
    (release 2.5 "seconds to fade by 60 dB after the note ends")
    (cutoff 6000.0 "lowpass filter cutoff in Hz, at middle C")
    (resonance 0.1 "filter resonance, 0.0 (none) to 1.0 (a mild peak)")
    (keytrack 0.5 "how far the cutoff follows the note, 0.0 (fixed) to 1.0 (fully)")
    (fenv-amount 0.0 "how far the filter envelope moves the cutoff, in octaves (-4 to 6)")
    (fenv-attack 1.5 "seconds for the filter envelope to rise")
    (vib-rate 4.5 "vibrato rate in Hz")
    (vib-depth 0.0 "vibrato depth in cents (0 to 50); it fades in over the attack")
    (drift 0.3 "slow random wander of pitch (up to 7 cents, and never less than 1.4) and morph, 0.0 to 1.0")
    (width 1.0 "stereo width, 0.0 (mono) to 1.0")
    (vel-sens 0.5 "how much velocity changes the level, 0.0 (none) to 1.0 (24 dB)"))
  (presets
    (strings (morph 0.2) (level 1.2) (attack 0.6) (decay 3.0) (sustain 0.9) (release 2.0)
             (cutoff 3500.0) (keytrack 0.6) (fenv-amount 1.0) (fenv-attack 1.2) (vib-rate 5.0)
             (vib-depth 6.0) (width 0.9))
    (ensemble (timbre 1.0) (attack 0.25) (release 1.5) (cutoff 9000.0) (resonance 0.15)
              (keytrack 0.4) (fenv-attack 0.5) (vib-rate 5.5) (vib-depth 12.0) (drift 0.2)
              (vel-sens 0.4))
    (cathedral (timbre 2.0) (morph 0.35) (level 0.9) (attack 1.5) (decay 4.0) (release 4.0)
               (cutoff 5000.0) (resonance 0.05) (fenv-amount 0.5) (fenv-attack 2.0) (vib-rate 4.8)
               (vib-depth 8.0) (drift 0.4) (vel-sens 0.3))
    (oo (timbre 3.0) (morph 0.1) (level 0.9) (attack 1.2) (decay 3.0) (release 3.0) (cutoff 3000.0)
        (fenv-attack 1.0) (vib-depth 5.0) (width 0.8) (vel-sens 0.3))
    (vowels (timbre 2.0) (morph 0.5) (level 0.85) (attack 2.0) (decay 4.0) (release 5.0)
            (fenv-attack 1.0) (drift 0.8) (vel-sens 0.2))
    (air (timbre 4.0) (morph 0.3) (level 0.9) (attack 2.5) (decay 5.0) (release 6.0)
         (cutoff 2500.0) (resonance 0.2) (keytrack 0.3) (fenv-amount 2.0) (fenv-attack 4.0)
         (vib-rate 0.3) (vib-depth 3.0) (drift 0.5) (vel-sens 0.2))
    (glass (timbre 5.0) (level 1.25) (attack 0.05) (decay 4.0) (sustain 0.6) (release 5.0) (cutoff 12000.0)
           (keytrack 0.3) (fenv-amount -1.0) (fenv-attack 3.0) (drift 0.2) (vel-sens 0.6))
    (frozen (timbre 5.0) (morph 0.6) (level 0.85) (attack 4.0) (decay 8.0) (release 10.0)
            (cutoff 8000.0) (resonance 0.05) (keytrack 0.2) (fenv-amount -1.5) (fenv-attack 8.0)
            (drift 0.5) (vel-sens 0.2))
    (organ (timbre 6.0) (level 0.9) (attack 0.15) (decay 1.0) (release 0.8) (cutoff 8000.0)
           (resonance 0.0) (keytrack 0.3) (fenv-attack 0.5) (vib-rate 6.0) (vib-depth 4.0)
           (drift 0.1) (width 0.6) (vel-sens 0.3))
    (sub (timbre 7.0) (level 1.05) (attack 1.0) (decay 3.0) (release 3.0) (cutoff 1200.0)
         (resonance 0.2) (keytrack 1.0) (fenv-amount 0.5) (drift 0.15) (width 0.5) (vel-sens 0.4))))

;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
;; the table geometry ;;
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;

;; Each table is N samples long, stored with three guard samples (N-1 before
;; the start, 0 and 1 after the end) so a cubic read never has to wrap.
(bind-val PADSYNTH_N i64 131072)
(bind-val PADSYNTH_BITS i64 17)
(bind-val PADSYNTH_LEN i64 131075)
(bind-val PADSYNTH_ZONES i64 14)
(bind-val PADSYNTH_TIMBRES i64 8)
;; a layer of a timbre's recipe is 48 numbers: see padsynth_layer_clear
(bind-val PADSYNTH_LAYER i64 48)

;; the bank, shared by every padsynth track and built once (padsynth_build)
(bind-val padsynth_tables i16*)  ;; 112 tables, timbre-major: table (timbre * 14 + zone)
(bind-val padsynth_gains SAMPLE*) ;; each table's gain, which brings its RMS to 1.0
(bind-val padsynth_bases SAMPLE*) ;; each zone's base frequency in Hz
(bind-val padsynth_trims SAMPLE*) ;; each timbre's loudness trim (linear)
(bind-val padsynth_built i64 0)
(bind-val padsynth_seed i64 0)    ;; a running count, which seeds each voice's randomness

(bind-func static padsynth_rand
  "a uniform random number in [0, 1).

The generator is SplitMix64 (Steele, Lea and Flood): a counter which steps by
a large odd constant, scrambled by two multiply-xorshift rounds. It's fast,
needs one 64-bit word of state, and a given seed always gives the same
sequence, so the bank comes out the same every time it's built."
  (lambda (state:i64*)
    (let ((z:i64 (+ (pref state 0) -7046029254386353131)))
      (pset! state 0 z)
      (set! z (* (bitwise-eor z (bitwise-shift-right z 30)) -4658895280553007687))
      (set! z (* (bitwise-eor z (bitwise-shift-right z 27)) -7723592293110705685))
      (set! z (bitwise-eor z (bitwise-shift-right z 31)))
      ;; the top 53 bits, as a double in [0, 1)
      (/ (convert (bitwise-shift-right z 11) double) 9007199254740992.0))))

;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
;; the inverse FFT, radix 2, in place ;;
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;

(bind-func padsynth_twiddles
  "the twiddle factors for an inverse FFT of size n: tw[2k] + i tw[2k+1] =
e^(2 pi i k / n) for k = 0 to n/2 - 1, worked out in double precision"
  (lambda (tw:float* n:i64)
    (let ((k:i64 0)
          (a:double 0.0))
      (dotimes (k (/ n 2))
        (set! a (/ (* 2.0 3.141592653589793 (convert k double)) (convert n double)))
        (pset! tw (* 2 k) (convert (cos a) float))
        (pset! tw (+ (* 2 k) 1) (convert (sin a) float)))
      void)))

(bind-func padsynth_ifft
  "an inverse FFT of the n = 2^bits complex numbers in z (real and imaginary
parts interleaved), in place: z_t = sum over j of Z_j e^(+2 pi i j t / n),
with no 1/n scaling.

This is the textbook iterative decimation-in-time algorithm. A transform of
size n is two transforms of size n/2, one of the even-numbered inputs and one
of the odd, joined by a 'butterfly' for each output pair:

  out[k]       = even[k] + w^k odd[k]
  out[k + n/2] = even[k] - w^k odd[k],    w = e^(2 pi i / n)

Doing that recursively all the way down to transforms of size 1 needs the
inputs in bit-reversed order (input 1 = 00..01 goes to slot 10..00, and so on).
So: shuffle the input into that order, then make log2(n) passes, each joining
pairs of transforms of size L/2 into transforms of size L."
  (lambda (z:float* tw:float* n:i64 bits:i64)
    (let ((i:i64 0) (r:i64 0) (x:i64 0) (b:i64 0)
          (tmp:float 0.0)
          (len:i64 2) (half:i64 0) (step:i64 0) (start:i64 0) (k:i64 0)
          (lo:i64 0) (hi:i64 0) (w:i64 0)
          (wr:float 0.0) (wi:float 0.0)
          (vr:float 0.0) (vi:float 0.0)
          (ur:float 0.0) (ui:float 0.0))
      ;; the bit-reversal shuffle: swap each pair once
      (dotimes (i n)
        (set! r 0)
        (set! x i)
        (dotimes (b bits)
          (set! r (bitwise-or (bitwise-shift-left r 1) (bitwise-and x 1)))
          (set! x (bitwise-shift-right x 1)))
        (if (> r i)
            (begin
              (set! tmp (pref z (* 2 i)))
              (pset! z (* 2 i) (pref z (* 2 r)))
              (pset! z (* 2 r) tmp)
              (set! tmp (pref z (+ (* 2 i) 1)))
              (pset! z (+ (* 2 i) 1) (pref z (+ (* 2 r) 1)))
              (pset! z (+ (* 2 r) 1) tmp)
              void)))
      ;; the passes: join transforms of size len/2 into transforms of size len.
      ;; The twiddle for output k of a size-len transform is e^(2 pi i k / len),
      ;; which is entry k * (n / len) of the size-n table.
      (while (<= len n)
        (set! half (/ len 2))
        (set! step (/ n len))
        (set! start 0)
        (while (< start n)
          (dotimes (k half)
            (set! w (* 2 k step))
            (set! wr (pref tw w))
            (set! wi (pref tw (+ w 1)))
            (set! lo (* 2 (+ start k)))
            (set! hi (+ lo len)) ;; (start + k + half), times two for re/im
            (set! vr (- (* wr (pref z hi)) (* wi (pref z (+ hi 1)))))
            (set! vi (+ (* wr (pref z (+ hi 1))) (* wi (pref z hi))))
            (set! ur (pref z lo))
            (set! ui (pref z (+ lo 1)))
            (pset! z lo (+ ur vr))
            (pset! z (+ lo 1) (+ ui vi))
            (pset! z hi (- ur vr))
            (pset! z (+ hi 1) (- ui vi)))
          (set! start (+ start len)))
        (set! len (* len 2)))
      void)))

;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
;; recipes: what goes into each timbre     ;;
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;

;; A timbre is up to three layers, each its own set of partials (or a band of
;; noise) with its own band widths, mixed at a set level. A layer is 48
;; numbers:
;;
;;   0 kind: 0 a harmonic series, 1 a list of (ratio, weight) pairs, 2 noise
;;   1 how many partials (series) or pairs (list)
;;   2 series stretch s: partial n sits at n^(1 + s)
;;   3 series slope a: partial n has weight n^-a ...
;;   4 ... times this for the even-numbered partials
;;   5 tilt corner in Hz (0 for none), 6 tilt order: a smooth lowpass
;;   7 band width in cents at middle C, 8 width exponent p (above),
;;   9 keyboard exponent: zone z's width is (7) * (base_z / 261.63)^-(9)
;;   10 level in dB, relative to the first layer's total power
;;   11, 12 noise: the pass band in Hz
;;   13 envelope floor (linear), 14 how many resonances, 15-26 up to four
;;      resonances as (centre Hz, half bandwidth Hz, peak gain linear)
;;   27-46 up to ten (ratio, weight) pairs

(bind-func static padsynth_layer_clear
  (lambda (l:double*)
    (let ((i:i64 0))
      (dotimes (i PADSYNTH_LAYER) (pset! l i 0.0))
      (pset! l 4 1.0)  ;; even partials at full weight
      (pset! l 13 1.0) ;; a flat envelope
      void)))

(bind-func static padsynth_series
  "a harmonic series of up to n partials (every one below the zone's limit
when n is 256), with weights n^-slope, even partials times even"
  (lambda (l:double* n:i64 stretch:double slope:double even:double)
    (pset! l 0 0.0)
    (pset! l 1 (convert n double))
    (pset! l 2 stretch)
    (pset! l 3 slope)
    (pset! l 4 even)
    void))

(bind-func static padsynth_pair
  "add a partial at ratio r with weight w to a list layer"
  (lambda (l:double* r:double w:double)
    (let ((i (convert (pref l 1) i64)))
      (pset! l 0 1.0)
      (pset! l (+ 27 (* 2 i)) r)
      (pset! l (+ 28 (* 2 i)) w)
      (pset! l 1 (convert (+ i 1) double))
      void)))

(bind-func static padsynth_noise
  "make the layer a band of noise from lo to hi Hz, shaped by its envelope"
  (lambda (l:double* lo:double hi:double)
    (pset! l 0 2.0)
    (pset! l 11 lo)
    (pset! l 12 hi)
    void))

(bind-func static padsynth_band
  "the layer's band width (cents at middle C), width exponent, keyboard
exponent, and level (dB)"
  (lambda (l:double* cents:double p:double kappa:double db:double)
    (pset! l 7 cents)
    (pset! l 8 p)
    (pset! l 9 kappa)
    (pset! l 10 db)
    void))

(bind-func static padsynth_tilt
  (lambda (l:double* corner:double order:double)
    (pset! l 5 corner)
    (pset! l 6 order)
    void))

(bind-func static padsynth_floor
  (lambda (l:double* db:double)
    (pset! l 13 (pow 10.0 (/ db 20.0)))
    void))

(bind-func static padsynth_res
  "add a resonance to the layer's envelope: centre Hz, -3 dB bandwidth Hz,
peak gain dB"
  (lambda (l:double* centre:double bw:double db:double)
    (let ((i (convert (pref l 14) i64)))
      (pset! l (+ 15 (* 3 i)) centre)
      (pset! l (+ 16 (* 3 i)) (* 0.5 bw))
      (pset! l (+ 17 (* 3 i)) (pow 10.0 (/ db 20.0)))
      (pset! l 14 (convert (+ i 1) double))
      void)))

(bind-func static padsynth_layer_copy
  (lambda (to:double* from:double*)
    (let ((i:i64 0))
      (dotimes (i PADSYNTH_LAYER) (pset! to i (pref from i)))
      void)))

(bind-func static padsynth_vowel_res
  "a formant between its low-voice and high-voice settings: w = 0 is the low
voice, 1 the high. Frequencies move geometrically, gains linearly in dB."
  (lambda (l:double* w:double f0:double b0:double g0:double f1:double b1:double g1:double)
    (padsynth_res l (* (pow f0 (- 1.0 w)) (pow f1 w))
                  (* (pow b0 (- 1.0 w)) (pow b1 w))
                  (+ g0 (* w (- g1 g0))))))

(bind-func static padsynth_vowel
  "the formants of a vowel (0 'ah', 1 'oo') for a zone based at bk Hz.

Rounded textbook formant averages, with the bandwidths widened about one and
a half times for an ensemble. Zones at C3 and below get the low-voice set,
zones at C5 and above the high-voice set, and the zones between are
interpolated."
  (lambda (l:double* vowel:i64 bk:double)
    (let ((w:double (* 0.5 (/ (log (/ bk 130.8)) (log 2.0)))))
      (if (< w 0.0) (set! w 0.0))
      (if (> w 1.0) (set! w 1.0))
      (if (= vowel 0)
          (begin
            (padsynth_floor l -45.0)
            (padsynth_vowel_res l w 700.0 130.0 0.0 850.0 150.0 0.0)
            (padsynth_vowel_res l w 1100.0 150.0 -5.0 1250.0 170.0 -6.0)
            (padsynth_vowel_res l w 2450.0 220.0 -18.0 2850.0 250.0 -22.0)
            (padsynth_vowel_res l w 3300.0 300.0 -28.0 3900.0 350.0 -32.0))
          (begin
            (padsynth_floor l -50.0)
            (padsynth_vowel_res l w 320.0 100.0 0.0 380.0 120.0 0.0)
            (padsynth_vowel_res l w 800.0 130.0 -12.0 950.0 150.0 -14.0)
            (padsynth_vowel_res l w 2300.0 200.0 -30.0 2650.0 250.0 -32.0)
            (padsynth_vowel_res l w 3000.0 300.0 -36.0 3500.0 350.0 -40.0)))
      void)))

(bind-func padsynth_recipe
  "write timbre tau's layers, for a zone based at bk Hz, into l (three
layers' worth). Returns how many layers there are."
  (lambda (tau:i64 bk:double l:double*)
    (let ((l0 (pref-ptr l 0))
          (l1 (pref-ptr l PADSYNTH_LAYER))
          (l2 (pref-ptr l (* 2 PADSYNTH_LAYER)))
          (n:i64 2))
      (padsynth_layer_clear l0)
      (padsynth_layer_clear l1)
      (padsynth_layer_clear l2)
      (cond
        ((= tau 0)
         ;; strings: a saw-like series under four broad body resonances and a
         ;; soft top, as a focused core (22 cents) plus a wide halo (70 cents,
         ;; widening towards the top) 9 dB down
         (padsynth_series l0 256 0.0 1.0 1.0)
         (padsynth_floor l0 -18.0)
         (padsynth_res l0 280.0 160.0 0.0)
         (padsynth_res l0 520.0 300.0 -2.0)
         (padsynth_res l0 1150.0 700.0 -8.0)
         (padsynth_res l0 2700.0 1600.0 -7.0)
         (padsynth_tilt l0 4500.0 2.0)
         (padsynth_band l0 22.0 1.0 0.25 0.0)
         (padsynth_layer_copy l1 l0)
         (padsynth_band l1 70.0 1.2 0.25 -9.0))
        ((= tau 1)
         ;; ensemble: brighter, with a broad presence lift at 3 kHz
         (padsynth_series l0 256 0.0 1.0 1.0)
         (padsynth_floor l0 -6.0)
         (padsynth_res l0 3000.0 3000.0 0.0)
         (padsynth_tilt l0 11000.0 1.0)
         (padsynth_band l0 12.0 1.0 0.2 0.0)
         (padsynth_layer_copy l1 l0)
         (padsynth_band l1 45.0 1.15 0.2 -4.0))
        ((= tau 2)
         ;; choir "ah": a bright source through the vowel's formants, in wide
         ;; (50 cent) bands, with a little breath noise through the same vowel
         (padsynth_series l0 256 0.0 1.2 1.0)
         (padsynth_vowel l0 0 bk)
         (padsynth_tilt l0 5000.0 1.0)
         (padsynth_band l0 50.0 1.0 0.3 0.0)
         (padsynth_layer_copy l1 l0)
         (padsynth_noise l1 150.0 12000.0)
         (padsynth_band l1 0.0 0.0 0.0 -22.0))
        ((= tau 3)
         ;; choir "oo": a darker source and a darker vowel
         (padsynth_series l0 256 0.0 1.6 1.0)
         (padsynth_vowel l0 1 bk)
         (padsynth_tilt l0 3000.0 1.0)
         (padsynth_band l0 45.0 1.0 0.3 0.0)
         (padsynth_layer_copy l1 l0)
         (padsynth_noise l1 150.0 8000.0)
         (padsynth_band l1 0.0 0.0 0.0 -26.0))
        ((= tau 4)
         ;; air: weak even partials (a hollow tone) in very wide bands, and
         ;; shaped noise only 4 dB below it
         (padsynth_series l0 256 0.0 1.0 0.6)
         (padsynth_floor l0 -18.0)
         (padsynth_res l0 900.0 700.0 0.0)
         (padsynth_res l0 2500.0 1500.0 -6.0)
         (padsynth_tilt l0 6000.0 1.0)
         (padsynth_band l0 90.0 1.0 0.3 0.0)
         (padsynth_noise l1 100.0 14000.0)
         (padsynth_floor l1 -20.0)
         (padsynth_res l1 1200.0 1500.0 0.0)
         (padsynth_res l1 4500.0 4000.0 -4.0)
         (padsynth_band l1 0.0 0.0 0.0 -4.0))
        ((= tau 5)
         ;; glass: six slightly stretched harmonics falling steeply (the
         ;; pitch), the first overtones of a free bar at 2.756, 5.404, 8.933
         ;; and 13.345 times the fundamental in very narrow bands (the glassy
         ;; ring), and a wide copy of the bar partials for slow sparkle
         (set! n 3)
         (padsynth_series l0 6 0.015 2.5 1.0)
         (padsynth_band l0 6.0 0.5 0.0 0.0)
         (padsynth_pair l1 2.756 0.70)
         (padsynth_pair l1 5.404 0.50)
         (padsynth_pair l1 8.933 0.35)
         (padsynth_pair l1 13.345 0.22)
         (padsynth_band l1 4.0 0.5 0.0 -2.0)
         (padsynth_layer_copy l2 l1)
         (padsynth_band l2 40.0 1.0 0.0 -14.0))
        ((= tau 6)
         ;; organ: drawbars 68 4040 023 (16', 8', 5 1/3', 4', 2', 1') at 3 dB
         ;; a step, in bands only 4 cents wide and equally wide in Hz
         ;; (exponent 0), so the pitch stays steady, plus a faint chorus copy
         (padsynth_pair l0 0.5 0.501)
         (padsynth_pair l0 1.0 1.0)
         (padsynth_pair l0 1.5 0.251)
         (padsynth_pair l0 2.0 0.501)
         (padsynth_pair l0 4.0 0.251)
         (padsynth_pair l0 6.0 0.126)
         (padsynth_pair l0 8.0 0.178)
         (padsynth_band l0 4.0 0.0 0.0 0.0)
         (padsynth_layer_copy l1 l0)
         (padsynth_band l1 18.0 0.8 0.0 -10.0))
        (else
          ;; sub: a soft triangle-like tone (steep slope, weak even partials,
          ;; a lowpass at 900 Hz) whose upper partials widen fast (p = 1.4),
          ;; and a pure sub-octave 6 dB down
          (padsynth_series l0 256 0.0 2.0 0.3)
          (padsynth_tilt l0 900.0 2.0)
          (padsynth_band l0 8.0 1.4 0.0 0.0)
          (padsynth_pair l1 0.5 1.0)
          (padsynth_band l1 3.0 1.0 0.0 -6.0)))
      n)))

;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
;; from a recipe to a spectrum ;;
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;

(bind-func static padsynth_shape
  "a layer's spectral envelope times its tilt, at f Hz"
  (lambda (l:double* f:double)
    (let ((e:double (pref l 13))
          (n (convert (pref l 14) i64))
          (i:i64 0)
          (x:double 0.0)
          (y:double 0.0)
          (t:double 1.0)
          (order (convert (pref l 6) i64)))
      ;; a parallel bank of resonances, each 1 / sqrt(1 + x^2): a peak of
      ;; its gain at its centre, 3 dB down at x = 1 (half its bandwidth away)
      (dotimes (i n)
        (set! x (/ (- f (pref l (+ 15 (* 3 i)))) (pref l (+ 16 (* 3 i)))))
        (set! e (+ e (/ (pref l (+ 17 (* 3 i))) (sqrt (+ 1.0 (* x x)))))))
      ;; the tilt: 1 / sqrt(1 + (f / corner)^(2 order)), a smooth lowpass
      (if (> (pref l 5) 0.0)
          (begin
            (set! y (/ f (pref l 5)))
            (set! y (* y y))
            (dotimes (i order) (set! t (* t y)))
            (set! e (/ e (sqrt (+ 1.0 t))))))
      e)))

(bind-func static padsynth_ratio
  (lambda (l:double* i:i64)
    (if (= (pref l 0) 0.0)
        (pow (convert (+ i 1) double) (+ 1.0 (pref l 2)))
        (pref l (+ 27 (* 2 i))))))

(bind-func static padsynth_weight
  (lambda (l:double* i:i64)
    (if (= (pref l 0) 0.0)
        (* (pow (convert (+ i 1) double) (- 0.0 (pref l 3)))
           (if (= (% i 2) 1) (pref l 4) 1.0))
        (pref l (+ 28 (* 2 i))))))

(bind-func padsynth_layer_power
  "a layer's total power in the zone based at bk Hz, before it's scaled: the
sum of its partials' squared amplitudes, or of its noise's squared envelope
over the bins it fills. Partials outside 20 Hz to flim, or more than 80 dB
below the layer's loudest, are left out (here and when the layer is added)."
  (lambda (l:double* bk:double flim:double jmax:i64 sr:double)
    (let ((n (convert (pref l 1) i64))
          (i:i64 0) (j:i64 0)
          (f:double 0.0) (a:double 0.0)
          (amax:double 0.0) (total:double 0.0)
          (nn (convert PADSYNTH_N double)))
      (if (= (pref l 0) 2.0)
          (let ((lo:i64 (convert (ceil (/ (* (pref l 11) nn) sr)) i64))
                (hi:i64 (convert (floor (/ (* (pref l 12) nn) sr)) i64)))
            (if (< lo 1) (set! lo 1))
            (if (> hi jmax) (set! hi jmax))
            (set! j lo)
            (while (<= j hi)
              (set! a (padsynth_shape l (/ (* (convert j double) sr) nn)))
              (set! total (+ total (* a a)))
              (set! j (+ j 1)))
            total)
          (begin
            (dotimes (i n)
              (set! f (* bk (padsynth_ratio l i)))
              (if (and (>= f 20.0) (<= f flim))
                  (begin
                    (set! a (* (padsynth_weight l i) (padsynth_shape l f)))
                    (if (> a amax) (set! amax a))
                    void)))
            (dotimes (i n)
              (set! f (* bk (padsynth_ratio l i)))
              (if (and (>= f 20.0) (<= f flim))
                  (begin
                    (set! a (* (padsynth_weight l i) (padsynth_shape l f)))
                    (if (>= a (* 0.0001 amax)) (set! total (+ total (* a a))))
                    void)))
            total)))))

(bind-func padsynth_layer_add
  "add a layer's power spectrum, times scale, into slot `slot` (0 for the real
parts, 1 for the imaginary) of bins 1 to jmax of the work buffer z.

bk is the zone's base frequency in Hz and beta the bin it sits on. Each
partial becomes a Gaussian band, exp(-((j - c) / h)^2) in magnitude, so
exp(-2 ((j - c) / h)^2) in power, centred on the even bin c nearest to it,
with h half its 1/e width in bins. The band's power is divided by its sum,
so every partial carries the same power however wide it is."
  (lambda (z:float* slot:i64 l:double* bk:double beta:double flim:double jmax:i64 sr:double scale:double)
    (let ((n (convert (pref l 1) i64))
          (nn (convert PADSYNTH_N double))
          (i:i64 0) (j:i64 0) (d:i64 0) (c:i64 0) (reach:i64 0)
          (r:double 0.0) (f:double 0.0) (a:double 0.0) (amax:double 0.0)
          (cents:double 0.0) (width:double 0.0) (h:double 0.0)
          (power:double 0.0) (sum:double 0.0)
          (g:double 0.0) (ratio:double 0.0) (q:double 0.0))
      (if (= (pref l 0) 2.0)
          ;; noise: every bin in the pass band, at the envelope's level. The
          ;; random phases (added later) make it noise.
          (let ((lo:i64 (convert (ceil (/ (* (pref l 11) nn) sr)) i64))
                (hi:i64 (convert (floor (/ (* (pref l 12) nn) sr)) i64)))
            (if (< lo 1) (set! lo 1))
            (if (> hi jmax) (set! hi jmax))
            (set! j lo)
            (while (<= j hi)
              (set! a (padsynth_shape l (/ (* (convert j double) sr) nn)))
              (pset! z (+ (* 2 j) slot)
                     (+ (pref z (+ (* 2 j) slot)) (convert (* scale a a) float)))
              (set! j (+ j 1)))
            void)
          (begin
            (dotimes (i n)
              (set! f (* bk (padsynth_ratio l i)))
              (if (and (>= f 20.0) (<= f flim))
                  (begin
                    (set! a (* (padsynth_weight l i) (padsynth_shape l f)))
                    (if (> a amax) (set! amax a))
                    void)))
            ;; this zone's width in cents: narrower up the keyboard when the
            ;; keyboard exponent is above 0
            (set! cents (* (pref l 7) (pow (/ bk 261.63) (- 0.0 (pref l 9)))))
            (dotimes (i n)
              (set! r (padsynth_ratio l i))
              (set! f (* bk r))
              (set! a (* (padsynth_weight l i) (padsynth_shape l f)))
              (if (and (>= f 20.0) (<= f flim) (>= a (* 0.0001 amax)))
                  (begin
                    (set! width (* (- (pow 2.0 (/ cents 1200.0)) 1.0) bk (pow r (pref l 8))))
                    (set! h (/ (* width nn) (* 2.0 sr)))
                    (set! c (* 2 (convert (floor (+ (* 0.5 r beta) 0.5)) i64)))
                    (set! power (* scale a a))
                    (if (< h 0.25)
                        ;; narrower than a bin: all of it in the centre bin
                        (begin
                          (if (and (>= c 1) (<= c jmax))
                              (pset! z (+ (* 2 c) slot)
                                     (+ (pref z (+ (* 2 c) slot)) (convert power float))))
                          void)
                        (begin
                          ;; Walk out from the centre. exp(-2 d^2 / h^2) for
                          ;; d = 1, 2, 3 ... is each step's value times a
                          ;; ratio, and the ratio itself shrinks by a fixed
                          ;; factor each step, so the band needs only two
                          ;; exps rather than one per bin.
                          (set! reach (convert (ceil (* 3.0 h)) i64))
                          (set! q (exp (/ -4.0 (* h h))))
                          (if (>= h 1.5)
                              ;; the sum of the samples of a wide Gaussian is
                              ;; its integral
                              (begin (set! sum (* h 1.2533141373155003)) void)
                              (begin
                                (set! sum 1.0)
                                (set! g 1.0)
                                (set! ratio (exp (/ -2.0 (* h h))))
                                (dotimes (d reach)
                                  (set! g (* g ratio))
                                  (set! ratio (* ratio q))
                                  (set! sum (+ sum (* 2.0 g))))
                                void))
                          (set! power (/ power sum))
                          (if (and (>= c 1) (<= c jmax))
                              (pset! z (+ (* 2 c) slot)
                                     (+ (pref z (+ (* 2 c) slot)) (convert power float))))
                          (set! g 1.0)
                          (set! ratio (exp (/ -2.0 (* h h))))
                          (set! d 1)
                          (while (<= d reach)
                            (set! g (* g ratio))
                            (set! ratio (* ratio q))
                            (set! j (+ c d))
                            (if (<= j jmax)
                                (pset! z (+ (* 2 j) slot)
                                       (+ (pref z (+ (* 2 j) slot)) (convert (* power g) float))))
                            (set! j (- c d))
                            (if (and (>= j 1) (<= j jmax))
                                (pset! z (+ (* 2 j) slot)
                                       (+ (pref z (+ (* 2 j) slot)) (convert (* power g) float))))
                            (set! d (+ d 1)))
                          void)))
                  void))
            void)))))

;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
;; from a spectrum to the tables ;;
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;

(bind-func padsynth_zone_limit
  "the highest frequency a zone of timbre tau may hold. A note reads a zone at
up to half an octave above its base (the top zone a whole octave), and the
result must stay below 0.45 times the sample rate. The glass and the organ
are made of separate lines, which show up as faint extra lines where the
cubic read is not exact, so their zones stop at 0.2 times the sample rate."
  (lambda (zone:i64 tau:i64 sr:double)
    (let ((lim:double (if (= zone (- PADSYNTH_ZONES 1))
                          (/ (* 0.45 sr) 2.0)
                          (/ (* 0.45 sr) 1.4142135623730951))))
      (if (and (>= tau 5) (<= tau 6) (> lim (* 0.2 sr)))
          (* 0.2 sr)
          lim))))

(bind-func padsynth_store
  "quantise the real (part 0) or imaginary (part 1) parts of z into table
`table`, with its guard samples, and set its gain so that gain * sample has an
RMS of 1"
  (lambda (z:float* part:i64 table:i64)
    (let ((n PADSYNTH_N)
          (t:i64 0)
          (x:double 0.0)
          (sumsq:double 0.0)
          (peak:double 0.0)
          (rms:double 0.0)
          (s:double 0.0)
          (dst:i16* (pref-ptr padsynth_tables (* table PADSYNTH_LEN))))
      (dotimes (t n)
        (set! x (convert (pref z (+ (* 2 t) part)) double))
        (set! sumsq (+ sumsq (* x x)))
        (if (> (fabs x) peak) (set! peak (fabs x))))
      (set! rms (sqrt (/ sumsq (convert n double))))
      (set! s (/ 32767.0 peak))
      ;; sample t goes in slot t + 1; slot 0 holds sample N - 1
      (dotimes (t n)
        (set! x (convert (pref z (+ (* 2 t) part)) double))
        (pset! dst (+ t 1) (convert (floor (+ (* x s) 0.5)) i16)))
      (pset! dst 0 (pref dst n))
      (pset! dst (+ n 1) (pref dst 1))
      (pset! dst (+ n 2) (pref dst 2))
      (pset! padsynth_gains table (convert (/ peak (* 32767.0 rms)) SAMPLE))
      void)))

(bind-func padsynth_build_pair
  "build two tables (zones 2m and 2m + 1 of timbre tau) with one inverse FFT.

The inverse transform of a spectrum with conjugate symmetry (X_(N-j) =
conj(X_j)) is real. Two such spectra X and Y can share one complex
transform: put Z = X + iY, and the real part of the result is X's table and
the imaginary part Y's. So the power spectra are built in the real and
imaginary slots of bins 0 to N/2, then each bin gets its magnitude and a
random phase and the upper half is filled in as the conjugates."
  (lambda (tau:i64 m:i64 z:float* tw:float* l:double* sr:double)
    (let ((n PADSYNTH_N)
          (half (/ PADSYNTH_N 2))
          (nn (convert PADSYNTH_N double))
          (slot:i64 0) (zone:i64 0) (layer:i64 0) (layers:i64 0) (j:i64 0)
          (bk:double 0.0) (beta:double 0.0) (flim:double 0.0) (jmax:i64 0)
          (p1:double 0.0) (pl:double 0.0)
          (rng:i64* (salloc 2))
          (mx:double 0.0) (my:double 0.0) (ax:double 0.0) (ay:double 0.0)
          (xr:double 0.0) (xi:double 0.0) (yr:double 0.0) (yi:double 0.0))
      (dotimes (j (* 2 n)) (pset! z j 0.0))
      (dotimes (slot 2)
        (set! zone (+ (* 2 m) slot))
        (set! bk (convert (pref padsynth_bases zone) double))
        (set! beta (/ (* bk nn) sr))
        (set! flim (padsynth_zone_limit zone tau sr))
        (set! jmax (convert (floor (/ (* flim nn) sr)) i64))
        (set! layers (padsynth_recipe tau bk l))
        ;; the first layer sets the reference; each other layer is scaled so
        ;; its total power is its level in dB relative to the first's
        (set! p1 (padsynth_layer_power l bk flim jmax sr))
        (dotimes (layer layers)
          (set! pl (padsynth_layer_power (pref-ptr l (* layer PADSYNTH_LAYER)) bk flim jmax sr))
          (if (> pl 0.0)
              (padsynth_layer_add z slot (pref-ptr l (* layer PADSYNTH_LAYER)) bk beta flim jmax sr
                                  (if (= layer 0)
                                      1.0
                                      (* (pow 10.0 (/ (pref l (+ (* layer PADSYNTH_LAYER) 10)) 10.0))
                                         (/ p1 pl)))))))
      ;; magnitudes and random phases, a fixed seed per table
      (pset! rng 0 (+ 1 (* 1000 tau) (* 2 m)))
      (pset! rng 1 (+ 2 (* 1000 tau) (* 2 m)))
      (set! j 1)
      (while (< j half)
        (set! mx (sqrt (convert (pref z (* 2 j)) double)))
        (set! my (sqrt (convert (pref z (+ (* 2 j) 1)) double)))
        (set! ax (* 6.283185307179586 (padsynth_rand (pref-ptr rng 0))))
        (set! ay (* 6.283185307179586 (padsynth_rand (pref-ptr rng 1))))
        (set! xr (* mx (cos ax)))
        (set! xi (* mx (sin ax)))
        (set! yr (* my (cos ay)))
        (set! yi (* my (sin ay)))
        ;; Z_j = X_j + i Y_j, and Z_(N-j) = conj(X_j) + i conj(Y_j)
        (pset! z (* 2 j) (convert (- xr yi) float))
        (pset! z (+ (* 2 j) 1) (convert (+ xi yr) float))
        (pset! z (* 2 (- n j)) (convert (+ xr yi) float))
        (pset! z (+ (* 2 (- n j)) 1) (convert (- yr xi) float))
        (set! j (+ j 1)))
      ;; no DC, and nothing at the Nyquist bin
      (pset! z 0 0.0)
      (pset! z 1 0.0)
      (pset! z n 0.0)
      (pset! z (+ n 1) 0.0)
      (padsynth_ifft z tw n PADSYNTH_BITS)
      (padsynth_store z 0 (+ (* tau PADSYNTH_ZONES) (* 2 m)))
      (padsynth_store z 1 (+ (* tau PADSYNTH_ZONES) (* 2 m) 1))
      void)))

(bind-func padsynth_build
  "build the bank: eight timbres at fourteen zones, 112 tables. This runs once,
when the first padsynth track is made; every later track shares the tables."
  (lambda ()
    (if (= padsynth_built 0)
        (let ((t0 (clock_clock))
              (sr (convert SRf double))
              (nn (convert PADSYNTH_N double))
              (ntables (* PADSYNTH_TIMBRES PADSYNTH_ZONES))
              (z:float* (halloc (* 2 PADSYNTH_N)))
              (tw:float* (halloc PADSYNTH_N))
              (l:double* (halloc (* 3 PADSYNTH_LAYER)))
              (k:i64 0) (tau:i64 0) (m:i64 0)
              (nominal:double 0.0)
              (beta:double 0.0))
          (set! padsynth_tables (halloc (* ntables PADSYNTH_LEN)))
          (set! padsynth_gains (halloc ntables))
          (set! padsynth_bases (halloc PADSYNTH_ZONES))
          (set! padsynth_trims (halloc PADSYNTH_TIMBRES))
          ;; zone k is nominally MIDI note 24 + 6k (C1, F#1, C2 ... F#7),
          ;; moved to the nearest bin which is a multiple of four
          (dotimes (k PADSYNTH_ZONES)
            (set! nominal (* 440.0 (pow 2.0 (/ (convert (- (+ 24 (* 6 k)) 69) double) 12.0))))
            (set! beta (* 4.0 (floor (+ (/ (* nominal nn) (* 4.0 sr)) 0.5))))
            (pset! padsynth_bases k (convert (/ (* beta sr) nn) SAMPLE)))
          ;; loudness trims in dB. Every table has an RMS of 1, but equal RMS
          ;; isn't equal loudness: these bring each timbre at middle C to
          ;; within half a loudness unit (EBU R128) of the others.
          (pset! padsynth_trims 0 (convert (pow 10.0 (/ 0.0 20.0)) SAMPLE))
          (pset! padsynth_trims 1 (convert (pow 10.0 (/ -0.5 20.0)) SAMPLE))
          (pset! padsynth_trims 2 (convert (pow 10.0 (/ 0.0 20.0)) SAMPLE))
          (pset! padsynth_trims 3 (convert (pow 10.0 (/ 0.5 20.0)) SAMPLE))
          (pset! padsynth_trims 4 (convert (pow 10.0 (/ -1.0 20.0)) SAMPLE))
          (pset! padsynth_trims 5 (convert (pow 10.0 (/ -0.5 20.0)) SAMPLE))
          (pset! padsynth_trims 6 (convert (pow 10.0 (/ 0.0 20.0)) SAMPLE))
          (pset! padsynth_trims 7 (convert (pow 10.0 (/ 0.5 20.0)) SAMPLE))
          (padsynth_twiddles tw PADSYNTH_N)
          (dotimes (tau PADSYNTH_TIMBRES)
            (dotimes (m (/ PADSYNTH_ZONES 2))
              (padsynth_build_pair tau m z tw l sr)))
          (free z)
          (free tw)
          (free l)
          (set! padsynth_built 1)
          (printf "padsynth: built %lld tables (%lld bytes) in %.2f seconds\n"
                  ntables (* ntables PADSYNTH_LEN 2) (- (clock_clock) t0))
          void))
    void))

;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
;; the voice ;;
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;

(bind-func static padsynth_read
  "table t at position pos (0 <= pos < N), by 4-point cubic (Catmull-Rom)
interpolation. Stored entries i to i + 3 are the samples at i - 1 to i + 2."
  (lambda (t:i16* pos:double)
    (let ((i:i64 (convert pos i64))
          (mu:SAMPLE (convert (- pos (convert i double)) SAMPLE))
          (ym1:SAMPLE (convert (pref t i) SAMPLE))
          (y0:SAMPLE (convert (pref t (+ i 1)) SAMPLE))
          (y1:SAMPLE (convert (pref t (+ i 2)) SAMPLE))
          (y2:SAMPLE (convert (pref t (+ i 3)) SAMPLE))
          (c1 (* 0.5 (- y1 ym1)))
          (c2 (- (+ ym1 (* 2.0 y1)) (+ (* 2.5 y0) (* 0.5 y2))))
          (c3 (+ (* 0.5 (- y2 ym1)) (* 1.5 (- y0 y1)))))
      (+ y0 (* mu (+ c1 (* mu (+ c2 (* mu c3)))))))))

(bind-func static padsynth_wrap
  "x, brought back into [0, n) (for 0 <= x < 2n)"
  (lambda (x:double n:double)
    (if (>= x n) (- x n) x)))

(bind-func padsynth_voice_c
  (lambda (p:SAMPLE* index:i64)
    (let ((rng:i64* (zalloc 1))
          (nn:double (convert PADSYNTH_N double))
          (halfn:double (* 0.5 (convert PADSYNTH_N double)))
          ;; the note
          (note:SAMPLE 60.0)
          (tau:i64 0) (tau2:i64 1) (new_tau:i64 0)
          (vel_gain:SAMPLE 1.0)
          ;; the two zone slots: which zone each holds (-1 for none), and its
          ;; left and right read positions and increment
          (za:i64 -1) (zb:i64 -1)
          (pal:double 0.0) (par:double 0.0) (pbl:double 0.0) (pbr:double 0.0)
          (inca:double 1.0) (incb:double 1.0)
          ;; where each slot's two timbres' tables start, and their weights
          (oa1:i64 0) (oa2:i64 0) (ob1:i64 0) (ob2:i64 0)
          (ca1:SAMPLE 0.0) (ca2:SAMPLE 0.0) (cb1:SAMPLE 0.0) (cb2:SAMPLE 0.0)
          ;; envelopes: the attack ramp, the amplitude, the filter envelope
          (stage:i64 2) (rho:SAMPLE 0.0) (ea:SAMPLE 0.0) (ef:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (astep:SAMPLE 0.0) (dcoef:SAMPLE 0.0) (rcoef:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (fstep:SAMPLE 0.0) (frcoef:SAMPLE 0.0) (sus:SAMPLE 1.0)
          ;; the filter, one per channel
          (s1l:SAMPLE 0.0) (s2l:SAMPLE 0.0) (s1r:SAMPLE 0.0) (s2r:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (fg:SAMPLE 0.0) (fk:SAMPLE 2.0)
          (a1:SAMPLE 1.0) (a2:SAMPLE 0.0) (a3:SAMPLE 0.0)
          ;; vibrato, drift and morph
          (vib_ph:SAMPLE 0.0) (vib_t:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (d1a:SAMPLE 0.0) (d1b:SAMPLE 0.0) (d1ph:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (d2a:SAMPLE 0.0) (d2b:SAMPLE 0.0) (d2ph:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (morph_s:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (morph_coef:SAMPLE (- 1.0 (exp (/ -16.0 (* 0.03 SRf)))))
          (level_s:SAMPLE 1.0) (level_t:SAMPLE 1.0) (width_s:SAMPLE 1.0)
          (width_coef:SAMPLE (- 1.0 (exp (/ -16.0 (* 0.02 SRf)))))
          (wide:SAMPLE 1.0) (narrow:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (glide (smoothing_coeff 0.02))
          ;; a retriggered voice still sounding fades out over 5 ms first
          (fade:i64 0) (fade_len:i64 (convert (/ SRf 200.0) i64)) (pending:i64 0)
          (tick:i64 0)
          (zone_j:i64 0) (k:i64 0)
          (f:SAMPLE 0.0) (t:SAMPLE 0.0) (w0:SAMPLE 0.0) (w1:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (wa:SAMPLE 0.0) (wb:SAMPLE 0.0) (m1:SAMPLE 0.0) (m2:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (mu:SAMPLE 0.0) (x:SAMPLE 0.0) (d1:SAMPLE 0.0) (d2:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (cents:SAMPLE 0.0) (fc:SAMPLE 0.0) (q:SAMPLE 0.0))
      (pset! rng 0 (+ 7919 (* 104729 index) (* 1299709 padsynth_seed)))
      (set! padsynth_seed (+ padsynth_seed 1))
      (lambda (v:Voice* out:SAMPLE*)
        (if (= padsynth_built 0)
            (begin (voice_done v) void)
            (begin
              ;; a new note: if this voice is still sounding a different
              ;; note (it has been stolen), fade that out first; if it's the
              ;; same note, swell again from where the envelope is
              (if (voice_start? v)
                  (begin
                    (set! x (padsynth_timbre p))
                    (set! new_tau (convert (floor (+ (clampf x 0.0 7.0) 0.5)) i64))
                    (if (> ea 0.0001)
                        (if (or (<> (voice_pitch v) note) (<> new_tau tau))
                            (begin (if (= fade 0) (set! fade fade_len)) void)
                            (begin
                              (set! rho (sqrt ea))
                              (set! stage 0)
                              (set! x (clampf (padsynth_vel_sens p) 0.0 1.0))
                              (set! vel_gain (pow 10.0 (* -1.2 x (- 1.0 (voice_vel v)))))
                              void))
                        (begin (set! pending 1) void))))
              (if (> fade 0)
                  (begin
                    (set! fade (- fade 1))
                    (if (= fade 0) (set! pending 1))
                    void))
              (if (= pending 1)
                  (begin
                    ;; start afresh
                    (set! pending 0)
                    (set! note (voice_pitch v))
                    (set! tau new_tau)
                    (set! tau2 (% (+ tau 1) PADSYNTH_TIMBRES))
                    (set! x (clampf (padsynth_vel_sens p) 0.0 1.0))
                    (set! vel_gain (pow 10.0 (* -1.2 x (- 1.0 (voice_vel v)))))
                    (set! rho 0.0) (set! ea 0.0) (set! ef 0.0) (set! stage 0)
                    (set! s1l 0.0) (set! s2l 0.0) (set! s1r 0.0) (set! s2r 0.0)
                    (set! vib_ph (* STWOPI (convert (padsynth_rand rng) SAMPLE)))
                    (set! vib_t 0.0)
                    (set! d1a (- (* 2.0 (convert (padsynth_rand rng) SAMPLE)) 1.0))
                    (set! d1b (- (* 2.0 (convert (padsynth_rand rng) SAMPLE)) 1.0))
                    (set! d2a (- (* 2.0 (convert (padsynth_rand rng) SAMPLE)) 1.0))
                    (set! d2b (- (* 2.0 (convert (padsynth_rand rng) SAMPLE)) 1.0))
                    (set! d1ph 0.0) (set! d2ph 0.0)
                    (set! za -1) (set! zb -1)
                    (set! x (padsynth_morph p))
                    (set! morph_s (clampf x 0.0 1.0))
                    (set! level_s (clampf (padsynth_level p) 0.0 4.0))
                    (set! width_s (clampf (padsynth_width p) 0.0 1.0))
                    (set! tick 0)
                    void))
              ;;;; the control rate: every 16 frames
              (if (= (bitwise-and tick 15) 0)
                  (begin
                    ;; vibrato, fading in over the attack (at least half a second)
                    (set! x (clampf (padsynth_attack p) 0.005 20.0))
                    (set! t (/ vib_t (* SRf (clampf x 0.5 20.0))))
                    (if (> t 1.0) (set! t 1.0))
                    (set! cents (* (clampf (padsynth_vib_depth p) 0.0 50.0) t (sin vib_ph)))
                    (set! x (clampf (padsynth_vib_rate p) 0.1 8.0))
                    (set! vib_ph (+ vib_ph (/ (* STWOPI 16.0 x) SRf)))
                    (if (> vib_ph STWOPI) (set! vib_ph (- vib_ph STWOPI)))
                    (set! vib_t (+ vib_t 16.0))
                    ;; two drifts, each gliding (along a half cosine) between
                    ;; random values 1.7 and 2.3 seconds apart
                    (set! d1ph (+ d1ph (/ 16.0 (* 1.7 SRf))))
                    (if (>= d1ph 1.0)
                        (begin (set! d1ph (- d1ph 1.0)) (set! d1a d1b)
                               (set! d1b (- (* 2.0 (convert (padsynth_rand rng) SAMPLE)) 1.0)) void))
                    (set! d2ph (+ d2ph (/ 16.0 (* 2.3 SRf))))
                    (if (>= d2ph 1.0)
                        (begin (set! d2ph (- d2ph 1.0)) (set! d2a d2b)
                               (set! d2b (- (* 2.0 (convert (padsynth_rand rng) SAMPLE)) 1.0)) void))
                    (set! d1 (+ d1a (* (- d1b d1a) 0.5 (- 1.0 (cos (* SPI d1ph))))))
                    (set! d2 (+ d2a (* (- d2b d2a) 0.5 (- 1.0 (cos (* SPI d2ph))))))
                    (set! x (clampf (padsynth_drift p) 0.0 1.0))
                    (set! mu (* 0.15 x d2))
                    ;; the pitch wanders by at least 1.4 cents, so that a held
                    ;; note does not run round its table exactly in step
                    (if (< x 0.2) (set! x 0.2))
                    (set! cents (+ cents (* 7.0 x d1)))
                    ;; the pitch
                    (set! f (* 440.0 (pow 2.0 (+ (/ (- note 69.0) 12.0) (/ cents 1200.0)))))
                    (set! x (* 0.5 (pref padsynth_bases 0)))
                    (if (< f x) (set! f x))
                    (set! x (* 2.0 (pref padsynth_bases 13)))
                    (if (> f x) (set! f x))
                    ;; the two zones either side of it, and their weights
                    (set! zone_j 0)
                    (dotimes (k 13)
                      (if (<= (pref padsynth_bases k) f) (set! zone_j k)))
                    (set! t (/ (log (/ f (pref padsynth_bases zone_j)))
                               (log (/ (pref padsynth_bases (+ zone_j 1)) (pref padsynth_bases zone_j)))))
                    (if (< t 0.0) (set! t 0.0))
                    (if (> t 1.0) (set! t 1.0))
                    (set! w0 (cos (* 0.5 SPI t)))
                    (set! w1 (sin (* 0.5 SPI t)))
                    ;; A slot keeps its zone (and its read positions) for as
                    ;; long as the zone is needed. A zone which isn't in
                    ;; either slot takes over the slot whose zone has dropped
                    ;; out; with a smoothly moving pitch that happens just as
                    ;; the dropped zone's weight reaches 0, so it's silent.
                    (if (and (<> za zone_j) (<> zb zone_j))
                        (if (<> za (+ zone_j 1))
                            (begin (set! za zone_j) (set! pal (* nn (padsynth_rand rng))) (set! par (padsynth_wrap (+ pal halfn) nn)) void)
                            (begin (set! zb zone_j) (set! pbl (* nn (padsynth_rand rng))) (set! pbr (padsynth_wrap (+ pbl halfn) nn)) void)))
                    (if (and (<> za (+ zone_j 1)) (<> zb (+ zone_j 1)))
                        (if (<> za zone_j)
                            (begin (set! za (+ zone_j 1)) (set! pal (* nn (padsynth_rand rng))) (set! par (padsynth_wrap (+ pal halfn) nn)) void)
                            (begin (set! zb (+ zone_j 1)) (set! pbl (* nn (padsynth_rand rng))) (set! pbr (padsynth_wrap (+ pbl halfn) nn)) void)))
                    (set! wa (if (= za zone_j) w0 w1))
                    (set! wb (if (= zb zone_j) w0 w1))
                    (set! inca (convert (/ f (pref padsynth_bases za)) double))
                    (set! incb (convert (/ f (pref padsynth_bases zb)) double))
                    ;; morph: smoothed, plus the slow drift
                    (set! x (padsynth_morph p))
                    (set! morph_s (+ morph_s (* morph_coef (- (clampf x 0.0 1.0) morph_s))))
                    (set! mu (+ mu morph_s))
                    (if (< mu 0.0) (set! mu 0.0))
                    (if (> mu 1.0) (set! mu 1.0))
                    (set! m1 (cos (* 0.5 SPI mu)))
                    (set! m2 (sin (* 0.5 SPI mu)))
                    ;; each read's weight: zone weight, timbre weight, trim
                    ;; and the table's own gain
                    (set! oa1 (+ (* tau PADSYNTH_ZONES) za))
                    (set! oa2 (+ (* tau2 PADSYNTH_ZONES) za))
                    (set! ob1 (+ (* tau PADSYNTH_ZONES) zb))
                    (set! ob2 (+ (* tau2 PADSYNTH_ZONES) zb))
                    (set! ca1 (* wa m1 (pref padsynth_trims tau) (pref padsynth_gains oa1)))
                    (if (< (* wa m1) 0.0001) (set! ca1 0.0))
                    (set! ca2 (* wa m2 (pref padsynth_trims tau2) (pref padsynth_gains oa2)))
                    (if (< (* wa m2) 0.0001) (set! ca2 0.0))
                    (set! cb1 (* wb m1 (pref padsynth_trims tau) (pref padsynth_gains ob1)))
                    (if (< (* wb m1) 0.0001) (set! cb1 0.0))
                    (set! cb2 (* wb m2 (pref padsynth_trims tau2) (pref padsynth_gains ob2)))
                    (if (< (* wb m2) 0.0001) (set! cb2 0.0))
                    (set! oa1 (* oa1 PADSYNTH_LEN))
                    (set! oa2 (* oa2 PADSYNTH_LEN))
                    (set! ob1 (* ob1 PADSYNTH_LEN))
                    (set! ob2 (* ob2 PADSYNTH_LEN))
                    ;; the filter: cutoff follows the key and the envelope
                    (set! x (clampf (padsynth_keytrack p) 0.0 1.0))
                    (set! fc (* (clampf (padsynth_cutoff p) 40.0 20000.0) (pow (/ f 261.63) x)))
                    (set! x (clampf (padsynth_fenv_amount p) -4.0 6.0))
                    (set! fc (* fc (pow 2.0 (* x ef))))
                    (set! x (* 0.45 SRf))
                    (if (> fc x) (set! fc x))
                    (if (< fc 20.0) (set! fc 20.0))
                    (set! fg (tan (* SPI (/ fc SRf))))
                    (set! q (+ 0.5 (* 1.5 (clampf (padsynth_resonance p) 0.0 1.0))))
                    (set! fk (/ 1.0 q))
                    (set! a1 (/ 1.0 (+ 1.0 (* fg (+ fg fk)))))
                    (set! a2 (* fg a1))
                    (set! a3 (* fg a2))
                    ;; envelope rates. A factor of 0.001 (-60 dB) over T
                    ;; seconds is exp(ln(0.001) / (T SR)) a frame.
                    (set! astep (/ 1.0 (* (clampf (padsynth_attack p) 0.005 20.0) SRf)))
                    (set! dcoef (exp (/ -6.9077553 (* (clampf (padsynth_decay p) 0.01 20.0) SRf))))
                    (set! x (clampf (padsynth_release p) 0.02 30.0))
                    (set! rcoef (exp (/ -6.9077553 (* x SRf))))
                    (set! frcoef (exp (/ -4.6051702 (* x SRf))))
                    (set! fstep (/ 1.0 (* (clampf (padsynth_fenv_attack p) 0.005 20.0) SRf)))
                    (set! sus (clampf (padsynth_sustain p) 0.0 1.0))
                    ;; level, and the stereo width: each channel is a mix of
                    ;; the two reads, scaled to keep its power for any width
                    (set! level_t (clampf (padsynth_level p) 0.0 4.0))
                    (set! x (clampf (padsynth_width p) 0.0 1.0))
                    (set! width_s (+ width_s (* width_coef (- x width_s))))
                    (set! x (sqrt (/ 2.0 (+ 1.0 (* width_s width_s)))))
                    (set! wide (* x 0.5 (+ 1.0 width_s)))
                    (set! narrow (* x 0.5 (- 1.0 width_s)))
                    void))
              (set! tick (+ tick 1))
              ;;;; every frame: envelopes
              (if (> (voice_gate v) 0.5)
                  (begin
                    (if (= stage 0)
                        (begin
                          (set! rho (+ rho astep))
                          (if (>= rho 1.0) (begin (set! rho 1.0) (set! stage 1) void))
                          (set! ea (* rho rho))
                          void)
                        (begin (set! ea (+ sus (* (- ea sus) dcoef))) void))
                    (set! ef (+ ef fstep))
                    (if (> ef 1.0) (set! ef 1.0))
                    void)
                  (begin
                    (set! stage 2)
                    (set! ea (* ea rcoef))
                    (set! ef (* ef frcoef))
                    void))
              ;;;; the table reads: up to two zones times two timbres, each
              ;;;; read for the left and the right channel half a loop apart.
              ;;;; (Per-frame temporaries live in this let, where the compiler
              ;;;; can keep them in registers.)
              (let ((ul:SAMPLE 0.0) (ur:SAMPLE 0.0) (yl:SAMPLE 0.0) (yr:SAMPLE 0.0)
                    (lp:SAMPLE 0.0) (bp:SAMPLE 0.0) (gain:SAMPLE 0.0)
                    (tabs padsynth_tables))
                (if (<> ca1 0.0)
                    (begin
                      (set! ul (* ca1 (padsynth_read (pref-ptr tabs oa1) pal)))
                      (set! ur (* ca1 (padsynth_read (pref-ptr tabs oa1) par)))
                      void))
                (if (<> ca2 0.0)
                    (begin
                      (set! ul (+ ul (* ca2 (padsynth_read (pref-ptr tabs oa2) pal))))
                      (set! ur (+ ur (* ca2 (padsynth_read (pref-ptr tabs oa2) par))))
                      void))
                (if (<> cb1 0.0)
                    (begin
                      (set! ul (+ ul (* cb1 (padsynth_read (pref-ptr tabs ob1) pbl))))
                      (set! ur (+ ur (* cb1 (padsynth_read (pref-ptr tabs ob1) pbr))))
                      void))
                (if (<> cb2 0.0)
                    (begin
                      (set! ul (+ ul (* cb2 (padsynth_read (pref-ptr tabs ob2) pbl))))
                      (set! ur (+ ur (* cb2 (padsynth_read (pref-ptr tabs ob2) pbr))))
                      void))
                (set! pal (padsynth_wrap (+ pal inca) nn))
                (set! par (padsynth_wrap (+ par inca) nn))
                (set! pbl (padsynth_wrap (+ pbl incb) nn))
                (set! pbr (padsynth_wrap (+ pbr incb) nn))
                ;; stereo width (the mix is worked out at the control rate)
                (set! yl (+ (* wide ul) (* narrow ur)))
                (set! yr (+ (* narrow ul) (* wide ur)))
                ;; the filter: a state-variable lowpass (svf_tick, from
                ;; dsp.xtm), stable however fast it moves
                (svf_tick yl s1l s2l a1 a2 a3 bp lp)
                (set! yl lp)
                (svf_tick yr s1r s2r a1 a2 a3 bp lp)
                (set! yr lp)
                ;; output
                (set! level_s (+ level_s (* glide (- level_t level_s))))
                (set! gain (* 0.07 level_s vel_gain ea))
                (if (> fade 0)
                    (set! gain (* gain (/ (convert fade SAMPLE) (convert fade_len SAMPLE)))))
                (frame_add_stereo out (* gain yl) (* gain yr)))
              ;; the note is over once it has been released and faded away
              (if (and (< (voice_gate v) 0.5) (< ea 0.0001) (= fade 0) (= pending 0))
                  (voice_done v))
              void))
        void))))

(bind-func padsynth_make
  (lambda ()
    (padsynth_build)
    (let ((inst (inst_make "padsynth" 12 (padsynth_nparams)))
          (i:i64 0))
      (padsynth_defaults (inst_params inst))
      (dotimes (i 12)
        (inst_set_voice inst i (padsynth_voice_c (inst_voice_params inst i) i)))
      inst)))
